// Adversarial scenarios, round 2 (architect, 2026-10-30): fresh seeds and new categories over the paths the first
// batteries covered (scenarios-approvals #282, the safety battery #284, routing #283), run against the real decision
// code, in memory, with a deterministic clock and an adversarial scripted model wherever the product calls one.
// Generated by tests/architect/scenarios/adversarial-r2-generator.ts (seeded). The end-to-end sample on real Postgres
// is flow-scenarios-adversarial-r2.test.ts.
//   A  spoofed approvals    quoted, forwarded, pasted, attributed, other-language, look-alike, invisible and reaction
//                           "yes"es through every approval path approve nothing (full-width letters: all or nothing)
//   B  split approvals      a yes cut across two messages approves nothing
//   C  approval context     a yes after the batch changed, in another chat of the same person, from another person in
//                           a reused thread id, after the window, or with two batches waiting approves only what that
//                           chat showed, still unchanged, or nothing
//   D  injection            instructions planted in postings, search results, email replies, resumes, file names,
//                           invites and pasted pages never cause an action, a confirmation, a kept instruction, a
//                           disclosure or a claim about the person (the brain's tools under an adversarial model; the
//                           reply reader under an adversarial model; the router reading an injected posting)
//   E  pressure             "you already agreed", false memory, role claims, urgency, impersonation, site automation and
//                           captchas, over several turns of the router: no action, no false value read back, no claim
//   F  cross-user           a tap on another person's card, a forged or another person's file link, another person's
//                           drafts on the send rail, another person's batch through a reused thread id: nothing
//   G  split secrets        a password or code typed after its label in the message before is removed; controls stay
//   H  brain replies        keys, a GPA never on record, another person's id and "I've sent it" never reach the person
// No network, no model: every model is scripted here.
